IMPORT prelude

-- Moneylenders Act 2008 (Singapore), ss 35 and 36, as filled in by the Moneylenders Rules 2009 (S 72/2009): the maximum rate
-- of interest and late interest (rule 11), the permitted fees (rule 12), the cap on interest, late interest and fees taken
-- together (rule 12A), the business-loan carve-out (rule 12B), and the unsecured-loan limits for licensees by annual income
-- (rule 21(1) to (4) and (6)).
--
-- Edition: Moneylenders Rules 2009, informal consolidation, version in force from 1 August 2026, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/MA2008-R1.txt (retrieved 13 October 2026). The rule numbers were read from the body of the
-- deposit; in the arrangement table the text extraction prints rule 11 as "1 1". The Act's ss 35 and 36 are as deposited
-- at ../../registers/source-bundle/MA2008.txt and encoded in ml-borrowers.l4; this module is a module of that row.
--
-- WHY. Added on 12 October 2026 for REQ-0277 (Haziq scenario, event from the Jun Hao scenario (supplied-fact entry)): a
-- licensed moneylender lends $8,000 to a borrower earning $36,000 a year in August 2032 -- the highest monthly interest it
-- may charge, and what fees.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: whether these Rules will still read this way in August 2032 (the deposit is the version in force from
-- 1 August 2026; later amendments cannot be known); revolving credit loans beyond the rule 12A(a) ceiling; exempt
-- moneylenders (rules 19, 20); excluded persons (rule 21A), foreign sureties (rule 21B), the foreign-borrower portfolio
-- limits (rule 21C); equal instalments (rule 10A); the note of contract, statements and receipts (rules 10, 13, 14); the
-- credit-bureau report that supplies the "outstanding unsecured loan amount" (s 66(5)(b)); the meaning of "unsecured loan"
-- where security covers part of the loan (taken as a supplied number); stamp duties and fees payable under other written
-- law, which s 35(3) leaves outside the permitted-fee limit; licensing fees (rule 5).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Moneylenders Rules 2009 -- interest, fees and unsecured-loan limits`

§§ `Rule 1A -- business loans`

-- Rule 1A(1): a "business loan" is a loan by a licensee to a company, an LLP, or a person registered under the Business Names
-- Registration Act 2014, in each case "carrying on business for, at least one year before the grant of the loan". Whether a
-- loan is one is a supplied fact here.

§§ `Rule 11 -- the maximum rate of interest and late interest`

-- Rule 11(1): "The maximum rate of interest mentioned in section 36(1) of the Act is the nominal interest rate of 4% per
-- month." (2): interest is "computed based on the monthly outstanding balance of principal remaining after deducting from
-- the original principal the total payments made by or on behalf of the borrower which are appropriated to principal."
-- (3): "The maximum rate of late interest ... is the nominal interest rate of 4% per month." (4), (5): late interest is
-- computed on the monthly outstanding balance of the amount "that is overdue", and "is charged only on an amount that has
-- fallen due and is not paid."
-- Rule 12B: "Rules 11(1) and (3) and 12A do not apply to a business loan granted by a licensee."
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum monthly interest rate` MEANS 0.04

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum monthly late interest rate` MEANS 0.04

GIVEN `is a business loan` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rule 11 caps apply` IF NOT `is a business loan`

GIVEN `original principal` IS A NUMBER, `payments appropriated to principal` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the principal on which interest runs` MEANS
    `original principal` - `payments appropriated to principal`

GIVEN `original principal` IS A NUMBER, `payments appropriated to principal` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most interest for the month` MEANS
    `the maximum monthly interest rate` * (`the principal on which interest runs` `original principal` `payments appropriated to principal`)

GIVEN `amount fallen due and unpaid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most late interest for the month` MEANS
    `the maximum monthly late interest rate` * `amount fallen due and unpaid`

-- Section 36(1) read with rule 11: a non-business licensed loan whose contract rate of interest or late interest is above
-- 4% a month contravenes s 36(1), and s 36(3) makes the contract unenforceable and the money lent irrecoverable.
GIVEN `is a business loan` IS A BOOLEAN, `contract monthly interest rate` IS A NUMBER, `contract monthly late interest rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contract breaches the interest cap` IF
        `the rule 11 caps apply` `is a business loan`
    AND (    `contract monthly interest rate` GREATER THAN `the maximum monthly interest rate`
          OR `contract monthly late interest rate` GREATER THAN `the maximum monthly late interest rate`)

§§ `Rule 12 -- permitted fees`

-- Rule 12(1): for "every loan (other than a business loan)", a licensee may impose, if "agreed to by the borrower":
--   "(a) a fee for each occasion of late repayment of principal or late payment of interest (including any late interest),
--        but not exceeding an aggregate of $60 per month;
--    (b) a fee, not exceeding 10% of the principal of the loan, that is payable when a loan is granted;
--    (c) legal costs incurred for the recovery of the loan, as may be ordered by a court to be paid to the licensee."
-- Rule 12(2): for a business loan: (a) a late-payment fee (no $60 limit); (b) a fee for each variation of terms at the
-- borrower's request; (c) a dishonoured-cheque fee; (d) a fee for each unsuccessful GIRO deduction; (e) for a term loan,
-- early redemption and early termination fees; (f) court-ordered legal costs. A business loan has no grant fee in the list.
-- Anything else is outside the permitted fees, and s 35(3) makes it irrecoverable.
DECLARE Fee IS ONE OF
    `a late payment fee`
    `a fee on the grant of the loan`
    `court-ordered legal costs of recovery`
    `a fee for varying the terms at the borrower's request`
    `a fee for a dishonoured cheque`
    `a fee for an unsuccessful GIRO deduction`
    `an early redemption or termination fee on a term loan`
    `an administrative or processing fee`

GIVEN `the fee` IS A Fee, `is a business loan` IS A BOOLEAN, `agreed by the borrower` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the fee is permitted` IF
        `agreed by the borrower`
    AND CONSIDER `the fee`
        WHEN `a late payment fee` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `court-ordered legal costs of recovery` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a fee on the grant of the loan` THEN NOT `is a business loan`
        WHEN `an administrative or processing fee` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE `is a business loan`

GIVEN `principal` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the largest grant fee` MEANS 0.1 * `principal`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the monthly limit on late payment fees` MEANS 60

GIVEN `late occasions in the month` IS A NUMBER, `fee per occasion` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the late payment fees recoverable for the month` MEANS
    IF `late occasions in the month` * `fee per occasion` GREATER THAN `the monthly limit on late payment fees`
    THEN `the monthly limit on late payment fees`
    ELSE `late occasions in the month` * `fee per occasion`

§§ `Rule 12A -- interest and fees together capped at the principal`

-- Rule 12A: "Despite rules 11 and 12, a licensee must not recover from a borrower of a loan, on account of interest, late
-- interest or any fee permitted under rule 12(1)(a) or (b), an aggregate amount exceeding -- (a) in the case of a revolving
-- credit loan granted on or after 30 November 2018 -- the amount that has been drawn down and not repaid at the time of the
-- recovery; or (b) in any other case -- the principal of the loan." Court-ordered legal costs (rule 12(1)(c)) are outside
-- the aggregate. Rule 12B: 12A does not apply to a business loan.
GIVEN `principal` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the ceiling on interest, late interest and fees` MEANS `principal`

GIVEN `principal` IS A NUMBER, `is a business loan` IS A BOOLEAN, `interest, late interest and fees claimed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount recoverable for interest and fees` MEANS
    IF `is a business loan` THEN `interest, late interest and fees claimed`
    ELSE IF `interest, late interest and fees claimed` GREATER THAN `the ceiling on interest, late interest and fees` `principal`
         THEN `the ceiling on interest, late interest and fees` `principal`
         ELSE `interest, late interest and fees claimed`

§§ `Rule 21 -- unsecured loans by licensees`

-- Rule 21(1): no unsecured loan (except a debt consolidation loan) to a Singapore borrower "whose annual income is less than
-- $20,000 if the total of" the new loan and the outstanding unsecured loan amount "exceeds $3,000". (2): to a Singapore or
-- foreign borrower "whose annual income is at least $20,000", the total must not exceed "6 months' income". (3): a foreign
-- borrower under $10,000 a year: $500. (4): a foreign borrower from $10,000 to under $20,000: $3,000.
-- (6): "annual income" is Y/3 x 12 and "6 months' income" Y/3 x 6, Y being the income in the 3 months before the month of
-- application; so 6 months' income is half the annual income. The outstanding amount excludes interest, late interest and fees.
-- (5): a contravening licensee is liable to a fine not exceeding $20,000.
GIVEN `annual income` IS A NUMBER, `is a foreign borrower` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the unsecured borrowing ceiling` MEANS
    IF `annual income` AT LEAST 20000 THEN `annual income` / 2
    ELSE IF NOT `is a foreign borrower` THEN 3000
         ELSE IF `annual income` AT LEAST 10000 THEN 3000
              ELSE 500

GIVEN `three months' income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`annual income from three months` MEANS `three months' income` / 3 * 12

GIVEN `new loan` IS A NUMBER, `outstanding unsecured loans` IS A NUMBER, `annual income` IS A NUMBER, `is a foreign borrower` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the unsecured loan is within rule 21` IF
    `new loan` + `outstanding unsecured loans` AT MOST `the unsecured borrowing ceiling` `annual income` `is a foreign borrower`
